From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: sm8550: power the QREF clock buffer

On SM8550 the UFS PHY's reference clock passes through a QREF buffer
(gated by TCSR_UFS_CLKREF_EN) that runs from LDO L1E. Downstream kalama
DTs give the PHY a vdda-qref supply with a 30 mA load; mainline has no
such supply, so L1E stays on only through its other users (DSI PHY,
PCIe PHY, eUSB2 PHY), and only the DSI PHY declares a load. With the
screen off the DSI PHY is disabled, the aggregate load on L1E is zero
and the regulator core drops it to LPM.

The UFS link is off in system suspend (spm_lvl 5), so a resume powers
the PHY up and recalibrates it while the screen is still off. With the
QREF buffer on an LPM LDO the SerDes PLL sometimes never locks:

  qcom-qmp-ufs-phy 1d80000.phy: phy initialization timed-out
  ufshcd-qcom 1d84000.ufshc: Failed to calibrate PHY: -110
  ufshcd-qcom 1d84000.ufshc: Enabling the controller failed
  ufshcd-qcom 1d84000.ufshc: ufshcd_host_reset_and_restore: Host init failed -5
  ufs_device_wlun 0:0:0:49488: ufshcd_wl_resume failed: -5

after which every I/O fails until a reboot (seen on the Odin 2 Portal
and the Thor). Add the vdda-qref supply with the downstream load, so
L1E is in HPM whenever the PHY is powered.

Kettle: untested on hardware when taken.

[ Kettle Linux kernel/patches/40-kettle/1402, body byte-identical ]
---
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
@@ -1299,9 +1299,16 @@
 	{ .supply = "vdda-pll", .init_load_uA = 18340 },
 };
 
+/*
+ * vdda-qref powers the QREF block that buffers the reference clock from
+ * TCSR_UFS_CLKREF_EN into the PHY. Without a load of its own the LDO falls
+ * to LPM whenever its other users declare none (DSI PHY off with the screen
+ * off), and on a resume from system suspend the SerDes PLL then never locks.
+ */
 static const struct regulator_bulk_data sm8550_ufsphy_vreg_l[] = {
 	{ .supply = "vdda-phy", .init_load_uA = 188000 },
 	{ .supply = "vdda-pll", .init_load_uA = 18300 },
+	{ .supply = "vdda-qref", .init_load_uA = 30000 },
 };
 
 static const struct regulator_bulk_data sm8650_ufsphy_vreg_l[] = {
